@section Error Handling
@cindex Error Handling

flexichain provides specific error types for different failure conditions.

@deftp {Exception} &flexi-position-error
Raised when an invalid position is accessed or specified.

@lisp
(module example-position-error (library flexichain))

(define chain (make-gapbuffer))
(flexi-insert! chain 0 "item")
;; This will raise &flexi-position-error:
(flexi-ref chain 5)
@end lisp
@end deftp

@deftp {Exception} &flexi-initialization-error
Raised when flexichain construction fails due to invalid parameters.

@lisp
(module example-init-error (library flexichain))

;; This will raise &flexi-initialization-error:
(make-gapbuffer :min-capacity -1)
@end lisp
@end deftp

@deftp {Exception} &flexi-incompatible-type-error
Raised when an operation receives an incompatible type.

@lisp
(module example-type-error (library flexichain))

;; This will raise &flexi-incompatible-type-error:
(flexi-insert-vector! chain 0 "not-a-vector")
@end lisp
@end deftp
